    22	   - There is a Las Vegas algorithm that, given a prime p, a primitive root g and h ∈ F_p^*, computes log_g h mod
    23	     (p − 1) in expected time L_p[1/2, c_DL(θ) + o(1)], uniformly in p.
    24	   - The constant is c_DL(θ) = min_{a>0} max(a + 1/√2, a + θ/(2a), 3a). This equals Theorem A's (1 + θ)/√2 whenever
