   170	- Σ_T n(T) = |S|² exactly. Each pair determines T = uv^{−1}, and no square-class condition is imposed.
   171	- The second-moment bound Σ n(T)² ≤ c_k|S|² is hypD Theorem S′'s count, steps 1–4, verbatim. It uses only
   172	  |uv′ − u′v| < Y² < p ⇒ uv′ = u′v and the shared-prime multiplicity count.
   173	- Cauchy–Schwarz gives #{T : n(T) > 0} ≥ |S|⁴/(c_k|S|²). Divide by p − 1. ∎
